§§ `Rule 1 -- definitions`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 69 r 1 kind of civil restraint order` IS ONE OF
    `o 69 r 1(a) a limited civil restraint order`
    `o 69 r 1(b) an extended civil restraint order`
    `o 69 r 1(c) a general civil restraint order`

-- src:7679 | 1. In this Order, unless the context otherwise requires — “Act” means the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969, and any reference to a section is, unless it is otherwise expressly provided, a reference to a section in the Act;
@ref O 69 r 1 “Act” (src:7679)
GIVEN `the enactment is the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 69 r 1 the enactment is the Act` MEANS
    IF `the enactment is the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): ""Act" means the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969"

-- src:7680 | “civil restraint order” means — ( a )
-- src:7681 | a limited civil restraint order;
-- src:7682 | ( b )
-- src:7683 | an extended civil restraint order; or
-- src:7684 | ( c )
