GIVEN `the order is a limited civil restraint order` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the order is an extended civil restraint order` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the order is a general civil restraint order` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 69 r 1 the order is a civil restraint order` MEANS
    IF `the order is a limited civil restraint order` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the order is an extended civil restraint order` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the order is a general civil restraint order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the order is a limited civil restraint order` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `the order is an extended civil restraint order` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `the order is a general civil restraint order` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): ""civil restraint order" means (a) a limited civil restraint order; (b) an extended civil restraint order; or (c) a general civil restraint order"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): at least one of the three kinds is not answered, so the closed list is not decided

-- src:7686 | “Court” means the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal;
@ref O 69 r 1 “Court” (src:7686)
GIVEN level IS A `Court level`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 69 r 1 a court is the Court` MEANS
    CONSIDER level
    WHEN `General Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Appellate Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Court of Appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `District Court` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): ""Court" means the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal"
