    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a party, against whom any order mentioned in section 73A(2), (3), (5) or (6) is in force, files any document in the legal proceedings in respect of which that order was made"

@ref O 69 r 5(3) (src:7715-7718)
GIVEN `o 69 r 5(3) this paragraph applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is any other party to those legal proceedings, or to the application pursuant to which that order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 69 r 5(3)(a) the person may apply for the document to be struck out` MEANS
    IF `o 69 r 5(3) this paragraph applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `the person is any other party to those legal proceedings, or to the application pursuant to which that order was made`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other party to those legal proceedings, or to the application pursuant to which that order was made"
    ELSE IF `o 69 r 5(3) this paragraph applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the "Where" condition is not met
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the paragraph applies is not answered

@ref O 69 r 5(3) (src:7715-7718)
GIVEN `o 69 r 5(3) this paragraph applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an application has been made under sub-paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court acts on its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 69 r 5(3)(b) the Court may strike out the document` MEANS
    IF `o 69 r 5(3) this paragraph applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `an application has been made under sub-paragraph (a)` OR `the Court acts on its own motion`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on an application under sub-paragraph (a), or on the Court's own motion"
    ELSE IF `o 69 r 5(3) this paragraph applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the "Where" condition is not met
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the paragraph applies is not answered

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 69 -- the duties as regulative rules`
-- ===========================================================================

-- The text states no number of days for these duties, so no rule below has a WITHIN.

DECLARE `o 69 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 69 the person that applies for the order`
    `o 69 the party applying for permission`

DECLARE `o 69 act` IS ONE OF
    `o 69 extract the order and serve it on all other parties`
    `o 69 serve the application and affidavit on the persons named`

-- src:7693 | 3. —(1) A limited civil restraint order, an extended civil restraint order and a general civil restraint order must be in Forms 99, 100 and 101, respectively. (2) A civil restraint order must be extracted by the person that applies for the order, and must be served on all other parties to the legal proceedings in respect of which the order was made. [S 206/2022 wef 01/04/2022]
@ref O 69 r 3(2) (src:7693)
`o 69 r 3(2) the duty to extract and serve the order` MEANS
    PARTY `o 69 the person that applies for the order`
    MUST `o 69 extract the order and serve it on all other parties`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 69 the person that applies for the order` BECAUSE "the civil restraint order was not extracted and served on all other parties to the legal proceedings in respect of which it was made"

-- src:7695 | 4. —(1) Where an extended civil restraint order or a general civil restraint order is in force against a party, an application by that party for permission to commence an action, and the supporting affidavit for that application, must be served — ( a )
-- src:7696 | on every intended defendant to the action; and
-- src:7697 | ( b )
-- src:7698 | if the civil restraint order was made on the application of the Attorney-General — on the Attorney-General.
@ref O 69 r 4(1) (src:7695-7698)
`o 69 r 4(1) the duty to serve the application for permission` MEANS
    PARTY `o 69 the party applying for permission`
    MUST `o 69 serve the application and affidavit on the persons named`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 69 the party applying for permission` BECAUSE "the application for permission and the supporting affidavit were not served on every intended defendant and, where the order was made on the Attorney-General's application, on the Attorney-General"
